WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:04.203
-Our next guest is the host of
the weekly web series

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.839
"Snugglestorm" that can be
found on his Instagram.

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:10.009
Here's one of our favorites,
the very funny Pete Lee.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:14.080
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.581
-Aww! Thank you so much.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:18.551
It feels so good to be
back here in Minnesota.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.120
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.091
Minnesota.
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:31.030
Here, let me scooch past you.
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.199
Oh, you better watch out
for that frostbite.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.735
It'll burn you like a bagel.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.539
Yeah.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.441
This is my wardrobe
for the evening.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:44.643
I wore a camouflage jacket.

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:49.148
Yeah, this is my woodsiest top.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.350
But I don't know if you guys can
tell by the shiny zipper.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.753
It's Lululemon.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:59.558
Yeah, I look like a dance mom.

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:06.199
I look like I should have
a chest tattoo of a Crock-Pot...

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.669
with potholders that say,
"Live, laugh, love."

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:19.712
Oh, it just feels so good to be
around people again.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.314
Do you guys agree with that?
Yeah.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.215
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:25.751
Oh!

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:27.753
I've been so lonely in COVID,
the other day,

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.989
my Bluetooth speaker was like,
"Ready to connect,"

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.258
and I was like, "Ah, me too."

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:37.130
I want to connect with people

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.364
that don't even want to
connect with me.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.666
I met my new neighbor
the other day.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.033
He's this burly biker dude.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:45.137
He goes, "What's up?
My name is Chainsaw Mike."

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:46.739
Yeah, and I didn't want
Chainsaw Mike to think

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.942
that I didn't also have
a scary Nickname.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.343
So I was like, "What's going on?

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.912
My name is Indoor Dining Pete.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:00.553
Yeah, I'm dangerous.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.323
I touch door handles
and everything."

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.062
I touch door handles,
but I touch them up top now.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:11.598
That's what I do.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.968
Right? I Michelle Obama
the door handle.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:18.371
Yeah. Other people go low.
I go high.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.908
But now, when I enter
into a restaurant,

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:26.980
I look like a stripper
who's starting her dance.

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:35.788
Like, I don't just enter.
I create an experience.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:42.895
And then, when I leave,
you know, I wipe it down.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.931
[ Imitates hissing ]

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:53.572
God.

00:02:53.572 --> 00:03:00.346
Oh! Have you guys seen this show
on TV called the news?

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.615
Oh, my God.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:07.419
It is the best season ever.

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:09.288
Wow!

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.856
I saw this thing
on the news that said

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:12.558
that if you just load up
on vitamin D,

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:15.061
you're basically bulletproof
to COVID.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.796
And I believe everything that
I see on the news.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.430
This lady sneezed right next
to me the other day.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.498
She was like, "Ah-choo!"

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:23.936
I went tanning.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:27.840
Yeah. I walked out of there,
I was like, "It's a tan-demic."

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:35.414
But look at me. I'm not tan.
I'm like a shade of pink.

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:38.751
Like, look at my rosy
Santa cheeks, you know?

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.953
Like, if somebody was like,
"What's your ethnicity?",

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.289
I'd be like,
"Uh, Himalayan sea salt?"

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:50.863
Pretty sure.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:53.866
But my favorite character
on the news is Bernie Sanders.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.301
I love him. Yeah. Oh, my God.

00:03:56.301 --> 00:03:58.437
I love him so much because
I'm a late sleeper,

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:02.675
and he looks like he is, too.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.977
But I just love the way that
Bernie Sanders talks.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.046
Have you guys
ever heard him talk?

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.682
Here's what it sounds like when
Bernie Sanders talks.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:15.188
Have you ever rolled luggage
over a brick walkway?

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.589
That's what it sounds like.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:22.261
Like, "Da-da-da-da.
Da-da-da-da!

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.796
We need healthcare for all.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.799
Da-da-da-da-da.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.500
The wealthiest 1%.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.705
Da-da-da-da-da-da."

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.073
Alright, thank you guys so much.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.675
You've been a wonderful crowd.
Thank you very much.

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:40.312
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:43.249
-My thanks to Tracy Morgan for
being here in studio!

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.883
We love you, Tracy!

00:04:44.883 --> 00:04:48.021
Sam Heughan, Pete Lee,

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.655
and The Roots right there,
everybody.

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.724
Thank you for watching.
Stay safe, everyone.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.293
Stay tuned for
"Late Night with Seth Meyers."

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:55.862
Good night, everyone.

